From 6592817d2473bffc14758e8349a8974a7e1c41b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hyperdrive Project <noreply@hyperdrive-project.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 04:46:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] Bolt: copied proposals for LiLiCorr rounds and
 corpus-seeded decoded history

Ignition: the shared parallel draft round accepts host-prepared copied proposals when its owner exposes
copy buffers (only Nemotron-H opts in here). A copied token replaces the learned draft at its position with a
point-mass proposal while every earlier position was also copied, so stochastic verification stays exact.
Nemotron-H speculative graphs bind the existing copy inputs (token ids, count, cursor, generation).

Helios: --history-seed PATH preloads the shared decoded history from a corpus (little-endian u32 ids,
u32::MAX ends each response) before admission; the window grows to fit the corpus. The lookup, expiry and
proposal path are unchanged. Requires --history-drafts.

Validation: 1219 Helios lib tests pass, including a new seeded-history test; Ignition modules import.
Limitation: not yet exported or measured on GPU; the copied-proposal path needs a Bolt re-export and the
voice acceptance eval before use.

